MIGRATION HOLD — deploy-functions.yml will not run while this file exists.

Why this exists
---------------
`deploy-functions.yml` runs `supabase db push` on every push to main. The
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN was expired from 2026-04-21 until 2026-08-21, so that
push has not succeeded in four months. The broken token was, in effect, the
only thing stopping 47 local migration files that are absent from the live
migration history from being applied in one batch.

The token is now rotated. The migrations have NOT been triaged. Until they
are, a single merge to main would attempt all 47 — including one that aborts
the whole push partway on a missing constraint, and three that mutate live
data (two of which only make sense as a pair).

See docs/MIGRATION_TRIAGE.md for the full classification.

How to lift the hold
--------------------
Delete this file and merge. That is the only step; the guard job in
deploy-functions.yml keys off nothing else.

Do NOT lift the hold until the repair commands in docs/MIGRATION_TRIAGE.md
have been run against production and verified.
